1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:38,204
you want to be when you grow up? That used to be my favorite question when I was a child because I wanted to be so many things. An artist, a writer, a stylist, a designer, a makeup artist. Basically something new at different points in my life. But looking back, the thing that made me interested in all these careers was actually the same. Storytelling, self-expression, having a voice and a medium. By the way, I incorporated storytelling in my life through journaling and documenting my life as if it was a story. And then I moved on to fictional stories by sharing them with my siblings

2
00:00:38,342 --> 00:01:04,700
Here I grew up and social media happened and I found a new place to tell my stories. At one point, I was writing a coming-of-age story about a boy discovering life through his relationships. And then I started writing for a Korean blog where my job was basically to write about fashion and K-pop. And mind you, this was way before BTS and K-pop demon hunters. So I was basically putting my reputation on the line just to tell some stories. I even got halfway writing a book

3
00:01:04,806 --> 00:01:13,012
about quarter life crisis because being in the 20s is the worst thing ever. Then I also did some freelance writing to pay for my midnight KFC cravings.

4
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:38,556
Somewhere along the way, storytelling also became my actual job. I went into marketing, communications, editorial work, and tech. I started researching stories, interviewing people, and writing for senior leaders. My job is to take complicated ideas, make them simpler, to actually make people care about them. So technically, I never stopped telling stories. I just stopped telling them in my own voice. Then AI happened, and now telling stories is easier than ever.

5
00:01:38,758 --> 00:02:03,932
but telling them in your own voice is so much harder. And lately, I can't help but wonder, what does Asma actually sound like now? So me coming here is partly a way to figure that out. I want to try a different medium, research different things, go down unnecessary rabbit holes, and then come back and tell you what exactly I find. Aajkul is mostly tech because of my job, but I'm also interested in anime, F1, true crime, movies, books,

6
00:02:04,038 --> 00:02:16,372
and mostly everything on the planet. So if you ask me, I'm not really sure where this is going, but I guess that is kind of the point. Anyways, hi, I'm Asma. I'm here to find my voice and tell some stories.

7
00:02:16,742 --> 00:02:22,272
This is finally over

